{"op":"set","id":"lew42-framework","key":"summary","value":"The owner's own no-build vanilla-JS object framework. Every saved thing is an Item (id, data, named Lists of child Items); item.set(delta) emits a delta event that bubbles to the root, whose Store writes one nested JSON line per change ({\"tasks\":{\"c3\":{\"set\":{…}}}}) to the root's append-only .jsonl file. Opening replays every line through set(). On the dev machine a recursive fs.watch plus a per-socket byte-offset tailer pushes new lines over one WebSocket per tab; record files are written through one Node entry point (Servex POST /api/item) that applies each line to a live root before appending. No conflict resolution, no sequence numbers, no snapshots; production is static and read-only.","by":"lew42-study","at":"2026-10-30T00:15:21Z","src":"persistence-sync/lew42/overview.md"}
{"op":"set","id":"lew42-framework","key":"status","value":"in-house, dev-only live sync; integration/data-shapes-2 (9ba46ee, 2026-10-28) ready to merge, not merged","by":"lew42-study","at":"2026-10-30T00:15:21Z","src":"https://github.com/lew42/monorepo/blob/9ba46ee87219cb9ac5b99b887f0869a5aa4c6895/public/framework/core/Session/tasks/data-shapes/plan.md#L118"}
